# Coordinate relay ownership and retire only owned routes

## Context

Design: `.collab/design/2026-10-19-c2c-t3-external-connector.md`.
Pending planned work. During execution follow bl-fix-many: read the full ticket, verify blockers, commit the claim, work in an isolated worktree, review/fix, run the c2c gates on build boxes, merge and close. No T3 source changes. Tests use x-p35/x-tuf, never the workstation's full suite. Actual just bi and service installation wait for the current candidate's successful P9.M2.E1.T001 buildbox gate.

## Requirements

- Integrate T3 aliases with the configured relay using one authoritative owner per alias/host/session. Reuse existing machine transport; never create a register/heartbeat fight or a per-thread connector process.
- Automatically advertise and renew eligible service aliases. Do not activate an unconfigured public relay.
- Route incoming remote DATA to the exact local target and preserve the reply alias@host_id. Use durable-before-ACK transport and bounded retries.
- Retirement/uninstall stops renewal and removes only exact service-owned routes. Use a verified existing release API or explicitly bounded TTL retirement, not an invented immediate revoke guarantee.
- Preserve foreign leases, ordinary c2c peers and pending mail through reconnection, relay outage, identity mismatch and repair.
- T001 confirmed the selected public relay (0.18.2 a0b52e4) defaults leases private and lacks an exposed owner publication API. Implement a narrow signed owner publication operation plus explicit service-owned advertisement intent through the existing machine connector; ordinary private peers stay private. Capability-gate remote readiness and record necessary reviewed/tested relay rollout. Do not use admin credentials or silently deploy.
- Include the configured shared sessions broker in machine connector discovery and preserve canonical sender@opaque_host routes in the existing outbox path. Retiring only stops renewal unless a verified owner revoke is added; current TTL floor is 24 hours after final renewal, distinct from 360-day alias ownership reservation.
- User chose https://relay.c2c.im for the installed services, but activation must not reroute local aliases. Test local direct delivery with relay disabled and enabled, and cross-host relay delivery. No new direct cross-host transport in this feature.

## Acceptance Criteria

- Isolated relay tests prove one owner, coexistence with machine relay connector, restart/re-registration, outage/backoff, inbound/outbound reply identity and retirement latency.
- Foreign ownership is refused without force-takeover. Local delivery remains available during relay outage.
- No hidden relay deployment is required; any necessary wire change is surfaced with a concrete compatibility/deployment gate.
- The x-p35/x-tuf live matrix can exercise both directions using ordinary c2c alias@host_id addresses.

## Lane

Relay files/tests may run independently after T004 when they do not overlap. Service hookup is serial after T005. Record exact ownership before fan-out.
